---
import SectionLayout from '@/layouts/SectionLayout.astro';
import { getRouteMeta } from '@/data/routes';
const meta = getRouteMeta('/agent-toolkit')!;
---

<SectionLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} theme="toolkit">
  <h1>Agent Toolkit — One source of truth → many assistants</h1>
  <p>
    <em>Composable AI agent capabilities for every major coding assistant.</em> 61 skills, 16 agents, 10 loops, 6 profiles.
    Instalación: <code>uvx --from agent-toolkit-cli agent-toolkit install && agent-toolkit doctor</code>
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="scene1">
    <h2 id="scene1">Escena 1 — Un catálogo, muchos asistentes</h2>
    <p>
      Capacidades se escriben una vez en <code>skills/</code>, <code>agents/</code>, <code>loops/</code> y se compilan al
      formato nativo de cada herramienta:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Claude Code</strong> — plugin marketplace</li>
      <li><strong>Muse Code</strong> — skills</li>
      <li><strong>OpenCode</strong> — agents</li>
      <li><strong>Cursor</strong> — rules</li>
      <li><strong>Copilot</strong> — instructions</li>
      <li><strong>Windsurf</strong> — rules</li>
      <li><strong>Pi</strong> — skills</li>
    </ul>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:0.5rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:1rem 0;">
      <span style="padding:0.4rem 0.8rem; background:#7C3AED; color:white; border-radius:999px;">skills 61</span>
      <span style="padding:0.4rem 0.8rem; background:#0891B2; color:white; border-radius:999px;">agents 16</span>
      <span style="padding:0.4rem 0.8rem; background:#EA580C; color:white; border-radius:999px;">loops 10</span>
    </div>
    <p style="color:var(--color-muted);">
      No todas las herramientas reciben archivos idénticos — cada una su formato nativo.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="scene4">
    <h2 id="scene4">Escena 4 — Swarm orchestration</h2>
    <pre
      style="background:var(--color-ink); color:#E2E8F0; padding:1rem; border-radius:8px; overflow:auto;"><code>Task
 ↓ Recipe: pair | team | full
 ↓ Role assignments (planner, implementer, reviewer, architect, QA, human)
 ↓ State machine → Worktrees (separados) → Handoff queue (outbox→queued→active→completed)
 ↓ Review → Human approval → Final report</code></pre>
    <p>
      Herdr y tmux son <em>backends de UI</em>. Toolkit posee la semántica de orquestación. Cambia entre vistas sin
      cambiar flujo.
    </p>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; margin:1rem 0;">
      <div style="flex:1; padding:1rem; border:1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius:8px;">
        <h3>Herdr</h3>
        <p>Rich workspace, tabs, status, handoff actions. Recomendado local.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="flex:1; padding:1rem; border:1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius:8px;">
        <h3>tmux</h3>
        <p>Socket aislado, sesión por run, ventanas por rol. SSH/headless.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agent-toolkit" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
        >Repositorio Toolkit →</a
      > · <a
        href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agent-toolkit/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer">Arquitectura</a
      >
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Seguridad y presupuestos</h2>
    <p>
      Budgets: tokens, costo, wall-clock, concurrencia, restarts, handoffs, artifact size. Secret redaction, path
      containment, aprobaciones humanas, push/release denegados.
    </p>
  </section>
</SectionLayout>
